      "side": 1,
      "message": "The earlier software workaround performed the CFLY precharge operation in the LN9310 hardware by using these 4 registers to modify a single command of the LN9310\u0027s internal startup sequence.  This new workaround moves the CFLY precharge operation off the LN9310 and into the EC firmware (see the ln9310_precharge_cfly function) to free up these 4 registers so they can be used to modify a second command in the LN9310\u0027s internal startup sequence (unfortunately the LN9310 only has registers for modifying a single command otherwise it could all be done through the LN9310 register configuration)\n\nThese 4 registers now modify the internal startup sequence of the LN9310 to use the precharged CFLY capacitors as decoupling of an internal node during the startup sequence which should help prevent an OV glitch from appearing on the LN9310 output even if the internal level shifter on SW1 glitches and pulls up on the C1PA/B nodes.",
      "revId": "1679193952ca30b8388ebdc25f14b90ed9aac7b9",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
